<title>SPAIN: Santander sells 1.0 pct Spain's Sevillana.</title>
<headline>Santander sells 1.0 pct Spain's Sevillana.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish bank Banco Santander SA sold one percent of the share capital of electricity firm Sevillana de Electricidad outside normal trading hours on Thursday, market sources said.</p>
<p>A spokeswoman for Banco Santander declined to comment on the transaction.</p>
<p>The 3.3 billion peseta sale to a foreign investor was reported to the Society of Bourses, the sources said. The three million shares were sold at 1,110 pesetas a share.</p>
<p>Sevillana shares closed up 15 pesetas or  1.36 percent at 1,115 with more than 940,000 shares traded.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 34 1 585 2151</p>
</text>
